  "answer_text": "**Mundra Port** is the largest private and commercial port in India. \n\nKey facts about the port include:\n\n### 1. Location\nIt is located on the northern shores of the **Gulf of Kutch** near Mundra, in the Kutch district of **Gujarat, India**.\n\n### 2. Ownership and Operation\nThe port is owned and operated by **Adani Ports and Special Economic Zone Limited (APSEZ)**, a flagship company of the Adani Group. It was India's first major private port.\n\n### 3. Economic Significance\n* **Scale of Trade:** Mundra Port handles roughly **11% of India\u2019s overall maritime cargo** and about **one-third of all container traffic** in the country. \n* **Cargo Milestones:** It is a major global shipping hub, recently making history by becoming the first Indian port to handle over 200 million metric tonnes (MMT) of cargo in a single year.\n* **Special Economic Zone (SEZ):** It is integrated with a multi-product Special Economic Zone, allowing businesses to set up manufacturing and logistics facilities directly connected to the port.\n\n### 4. Port Infrastructure & Capabilities\n* **Deep-Draft & All-Weather:** It is a deep-draft, all-weather port, which allows it to dock some of the world's largest cargo and container ships (such as the massive *MSC Anna*, which docked there in 2024).\n* **Cargo Types:** It handles dry bulk, liquid cargo, crude oil, and containers. It also features the world's largest coal import terminal.\n* **Connectivity:** The port is highly integrated with India's national railway and highway networks, facilitating the quick transport of goods to landlocked northern and western regions of India.",
